00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:10.200
to both the platform and also even, for instance, iOS 26,

56
00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:13.720
very different APIs that you might have to interact with.

57
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.800
In addition, something that is a little bit different on mobile

58
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.240
is Apple and Android are much more cavalier.

59
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.240
They still try to do a good job being backwards compatible,

60
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.200
but there are breaking changes that happen.

61
00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.480
Version to version.

62
00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.680
If you are developing on the early days of Swift, you might remember

63
00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.280
you know, migrations from Swift one to Swift two to Swift three.

64
00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.800
It was just like completely different.

65
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.560
They even had to build tools to help you migrate.

66
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.240
And this was before, agents.

67
00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.240
So you kind of had to try to do it deterministically.

68
00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.920
So there's these yearly major releases

69
00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.920
again, often introduce breaking changes,

70
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.080
regular API deprecation for old versions.

71
00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.880
And in my experience, they do their best.

72
00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.280
But a lot of the nuances and details of the platform

73
00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.400
APIs are often not documented, and because you don't have access to them,

74
00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.560
the community also has a lot of trouble understanding what's going on.

75
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.880
So just a quick overview.

76
00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.240
Finally, some things to think about as you,

77
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.440
are putting together your

78
00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.680
plans for building a mobile app is there's much more device fragmentation.

79
00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.200
I didn't even put on here.

80
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.400
These are all, you know, form factors you might have to think about for iOS.

