83
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.000
So there's phone tablet and watch form factors.

84
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.520
And then on top of that there's also different UX paradigms

85
00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.640
that they really try to emphasize for these different form factors.

86
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.800
So we'll talk a little bit about how you might, deal

87
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.800
with that or reduce the scope to make the agent more successful.

88
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.160
And finally, something to consider is people now,

89
00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:59.240
some still upgrade their phones yearly, but your devices tend to be locked to

90
00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.120
a certain OS version, maximum OS version to encourage you to buy new ones.

91
00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.000
And so especially if you're targeting markets,

92
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.080
where people have less data access or are more price

93
00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.160
conscious, they might be on older devices and older versions.

94
00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.560
So that's also something to think about.

95
00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.960
And then finally something that I work on day to day,

96
00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:25.600
I think about a lot is mobile just has slow verification loops on web.

97
00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.440
You can load up a web page.

98
00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.560
Agents even can access them directly.

99
00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:33.080
But on mobile you're using custom proprietary toolchains

100
00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:39.120
and we're still seeing, new releases and new ways to access this for agents.

101
00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:44.560
So it's kind of a work in progress, a big one that you all might feel,

102
00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.880
at least if you are in the React or React native world and going to vanilla iOS is,

103
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.480
there's no hot reloading.

104
00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:56.560
There are some tools that make it easier, but basically you have to write your code

105
00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.880
on a build which may or may not take a couple minutes

106
00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.400
and then look at a real simulator or even a real device and try and verify

107
00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.600
your code is working so that whole loop is just slower,

108
00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:13.000
which produces more errors, and more reliability problems.

109
00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:14.720
We'll talk about

110
00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.720
a little bit of this too, but, you know, on web you have headless mode,

111
00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.720
so you can test UI without actually,

112
00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:26.440
running it in a true, iOS environment.

113
00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.240
You can't do that on iOS.

114
00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.560
You also can't replicate certain multitouch gestures.

115
00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:36.280
And finally, if you're testing things like Bluetooth or location based,

116
00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.400
capabilities, you have to use a real device.

117
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.280
So lots of complexity.

